characterRep -- extract the character of a polynomial GL-representation from its matrix
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        characterRep F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a square matrix over a
        polynomial ring $R[w_1, \ldots, w_{d^2}]$ representing a polynomial
        $GL_d$-action on some module; typically the output of *note schur:
        schur, applied to a generic matrix
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the trace of the
        diagonal specialization of F in a fresh polynomial ring
        $\mathbb{Q}[x_0, \ldots, x_{d-1}]$

Description
===========

Given a matrix $F$ whose entries are polynomials in the $d^2$ variables of a
generic matrix on $V = \mathbb{Q}^d$, characterRep substitutes a diagonal
matrix $\mathrm{diag}(x_0, \ldots, x_{d-1})$ for that generic matrix and reads
off the trace.  The result is the character of the $GL_d$-representation $F$
encodes.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[w_1..w_9];                                |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = genericMatrix(R, 3, 3);                      |
|                                                      |
|             3      3                                 |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = schur({2,1}, G);                             |
|                                                      |
|             8      8                                 |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : characterRep F                                   |
|                                                      |
|      2        2    2                2        2      2|
|o4 = x x  + x x  + x x  + 2x x x  + x x  + x x  + x x |
|      0 1    0 1    0 2     0 1 2    1 2    0 2    1 2|
|                                                      |
|o4 : QQ[x ..x ]                                       |
|         0   2                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : splitCharacter characterRep F                    |
|                                                      |
|o5 = s                                                |
|      2,1                                             |
|                                                      |
|o5 : schurRing (QQ, s, 3)                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note character: character, -- the character of a composition of Schur
    functors on GL(V)
  * *note splitCharacter: splitCharacter, -- decompose a symmetric polynomial
    into Schur functions
  * *note decomposeRep: decomposeRep, -- decompose a polynomial
    GL-representation into irreducible subspaces
  * *note schur: schur, -- the Schur functor applied to a matrix

