conjugate(WeylFilling) -- transpose of a Weyl-stored Young tableau
******************************************************************

  * Function: *note conjugate: (Macaulay2Doc)conjugate,
  * Usage: 
        conjugate T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling,, the tableau of
        conjugate shape, stored row-wise (so its rows are the columns of T)

Description
===========

Conjugation of a WeylFilling is the combinatorial transpose of the underlying
Young tableau, preserving the row-wise storage convention.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : T = weyl {{0,2,4},{1,3,5}}|
|                               |
|     +-+-+-+                   |
|o1 = |0|2|4|                   |
|     |1|3|5|                   |
|     +-+-+-+                   |
|                               |
|o1 : WeylFilling               |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : conjugate T               |
|                               |
|     +-+-+                     |
|o2 = |0|1|                     |
|     |2|3|                     |
|     |4|5|                     |
|     +-+-+                     |
|                               |
|o2 : WeylFilling               |
+-------------------------------+

The conjugate stores the columns of $T$ as its rows; equivalently, toList
conjugate T equals the list of columns of T, each sorted in its natural
top-to-bottom order.

See also
========

  * *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling, -- a Young tableau stored row-wise for the
    Weyl-module basis
  * *note conjugate(Filling): conjugate_lpFilling_rp, -- transpose of a Young
    tableau

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note conjugate(WeylFilling): conjugate_lpWeylFilling_rp, -- transpose of a
    Weyl-stored Young tableau
