isStandard -- test whether a Filling is semistandard
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isStandard T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note Filling: Filling,, assumed to have
        strictly increasing columns (for example, the output of *note
        normalize: normalize,); the routine scans adjacent columns right to
        left for the first row-ascent violation
  * Outputs:
      * null if T is semistandard (entries weakly increase along every row),
        otherwise a pair (i, j) such that T#i#j > T#(i+1)#j

Description
===========

In the combinatorial literature a semistandard Young tableau is a filling with
entries strictly increasing down columns and weakly increasing along rows.
This package calls such a filling standard; isStandard is its predicate.

The return value on failure is the Garnir-violation location used by the
straightening algorithm *note straighten: straighten, and by the main
Schur-module construction *note schurModule: schurModule,.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : isStandard new Filling from {{0,1}, {1,2}}|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isStandard new Filling from {{1,2}, {0,1}}|
|                                               |
|o2 = (0, 0)                                    |
|                                               |
|o2 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+

To enumerate all semistandard fillings of a given shape with entries in
$\{0,\ldots,d-1\}$, use *note standardTableaux: standardTableaux,.

See also
========

  * *note Filling: Filling, -- a Young tableau stored column-wise
  * *note normalize: normalize, -- sort each column of a Filling, with Koszul
    sign
  * *note standardTableaux: standardTableaux, -- all semistandard Young
    tableaux of a given shape
  * *note straighten: straighten, -- straighten a filling into a linear
    combination of semistandard tableaux
  * *note schurModule: schurModule, -- Schur module of a partition applied to a
    free module

Ways to use isStandard:
=======================

  * "isStandard(Filling)"

