isWeylStandard -- test whether a WeylFilling is Weyl-semistandard
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isWeylStandard T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling,, assumed to
        have rows in sorted (weakly-increasing) order, for example the output
        of *note weylNormalize: weylNormalize,
  * Outputs:
      * null if T is Weyl-standard (columns strictly increasing top-to-bottom),
        otherwise a pair (i, j) giving the first column violation: T#i#j >=
        T#(i+1)#j, scanning rows from bottom to top

Description
===========

A WeylFilling is Weyl-standard when, in addition to having sorted rows, every
column is strictly increasing top-to-bottom.  This is exactly the semistandard
condition, phrased for row-wise storage.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : isWeylStandard weyl {{0,1}, {1,2}}                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isWeylStandard weyl {{1,2}, {1,3}}   -- column 0: 1 >= 1 violates|
|                                                                      |
|o2 = (0, 0)                                                           |
|                                                                      |
|o2 : Sequence                                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

To straighten a non-standard WeylFilling into a linear combination of standard
ones, use *note towardWeylStandard: towardWeylStandard, (single step) or *note
weylStraighten: weylStraighten, (full reduction).

See also
========

  * *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling, -- a Young tableau stored row-wise for the
    Weyl-module basis
  * *note weylNormalize: weylNormalize, -- sort each row of a WeylFilling into
    weakly-increasing order
  * *note towardWeylStandard: towardWeylStandard, -- a single Garnir-style
    straightening step for Weyl fillings
  * *note weylStraighten: weylStraighten, -- straighten a Weyl filling into a
    linear combination of Weyl-semistandard tableaux
  * *note standardWeylTableaux: standardWeylTableaux, -- all Weyl-semistandard
    tableaux of a given shape

