printSchurModuleElement -- display a Schur-module element as a linear combination of tableaux
*********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        printSchurModuleElement(v, M)
  * Inputs:
      * v, a *note vector: (Macaulay2Doc)Vector,, a vector in a Schur module M
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a Schur module returned by
        *note schurModule: schurModule,

Description
===========

Interprets v as an element of M and prints it as a sum $\sum_T c_T \cdot T$
over semistandard fillings $T$ in the cached basis of M, with each T drawn via
its net method.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = schurModule({2,1}, QQ^3);                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : v = sum(numgens M, i -> (i+1) * M_i);                      |
|                                                                |
|       8                                                        |
|o2 : QQ                                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : printSchurModuleElement(v, M)                              |
|  +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+ |
|1*|0|0| 2*|0|1| 3*|0|2| 4*|0|0| 5*|0|1| 6*|0|2| 7*|1|1| 8*|1|2| |
|  |1| |   |1| |   |1| |   |2| |   |2| |   |2| |   |2| |   |2| | |
|  +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+   +-+-+ |
|                                                                |
|o3 = stdio                                                      |
|                                                                |
|o3 : File                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

