splitCharacter -- decompose a symmetric polynomial into Schur functions
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        splitCharacter(p)
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a symmetric
        polynomial in the eigenvalues of the diagonal torus
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the expansion of p as
        a $\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$-linear combination of Schur functions
        $s_\lambda$

Description
===========

Together with *note character: character, this gives the isotypic decomposition
of a polynomial $GL_d$-representation $W$ whose character is p: $$\chi_W =
\sum_\lambda m_\lambda \cdot s_\lambda \;\Longleftrightarrow\; W \cong
\bigoplus_\lambda S_\lambda(V)^{\oplus m_\lambda}.$$ The coefficients
$m_\lambda$ are the multiplicities of the irreducible polynomial
$GL_d$-representations in $W$.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : c = character({{1,1,1}, {2}}, 4);|
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : splitCharacter c                 |
|                                      |
|o2 = s      + s                       |
|      4,1,1    3,3                    |
|                                      |
|o2 : schurRing (QQ, s, 4)             |
+--------------------------------------+

Verifies the Hermite-reciprocity / plethysm identity $\wedge^3(S^2 V_4) =
S_{(4,1,1)}(V_4) \oplus S_{(3,3)}(V_4)$.

See also
========

  * *note character: character, -- the character of a composition of Schur
    functors on GL(V)
  * *note weylCharacter: weylCharacter, -- the character of a composition of
    Weyl functors on GL(V)
  * *note decomposeRep: decomposeRep, -- decompose a polynomial
    GL-representation into irreducible subspaces

Ways to use splitCharacter:
===========================

  * "splitCharacter(RingElement)"

