standardTableaux -- all semistandard Young tableaux of a given shape
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        standardTableaux(d, mu)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of the alphabet
        $\{0,\ldots,d-1\}$
      * mu, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a partition giving the column
        lengths of the *note Filling: Filling, (equivalently, the conjugate of
        the row shape $\lambda$; see *note schurModule: schurModule,)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, all semistandard *note Filling:
        Filling,s with column lengths $\mu$ and entries in $\{0,\ldots,d-1\}$

Description
===========

The output is a $\mathbb{Z}$-basis of *note schurModule: schurModule,(mu, R^d);
its cardinality equals the Weyl dimension $\dim S_\mu(\mathbb{Q}^d)$, given by
the hook-content formula $$\dim S_\mu(\mathbb{Q}^d) = \prod_{(i,j)\in\mu}
\frac{d - i + j}{h(i,j)},$$ where $h(i,j)$ is the hook length at cell $(i,j)$.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = standardTableaux(3, {2,1});|
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : #S                             |
|                                    |
|o2 = 8                              |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : rank schurModule({2,1}, QQ^3)  |
|                                    |
|o3 = 8                              |
+------------------------------------+

For $\mu = (2,1)$ and $d = 3$ the hook-content formula gives $(3 \cdot 4 \cdot
2)/(3 \cdot 1 \cdot 1) = 8$.

+-------------------------------+
|i4 : standardTableaux(2, {1,1})|
|                               |
|      +-+-+  +-+-+  +-+-+      |
|o4 = {|0|0|, |0|1|, |1|1|}     |
|      +-+-+  +-+-+  +-+-+      |
|                               |
|o4 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i5 : standardTableaux(4, {3})  |
|                               |
|      +-+  +-+  +-+  +-+       |
|o5 = {|0|, |0|, |0|, |1|}      |
|      |1|  |1|  |2|  |2|       |
|      |2|  |3|  |3|  |3|       |
|      +-+  +-+  +-+  +-+       |
|                               |
|o5 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Filling: Filling, -- a Young tableau stored column-wise
  * *note isStandard: isStandard, -- test whether a Filling is semistandard
  * *note schurModule: schurModule, -- Schur module of a partition applied to a
    free module
  * *note standardWeylTableaux: standardWeylTableaux, -- all Weyl-semistandard
    tableaux of a given shape

