towardWeylStandard -- a single Garnir-style straightening step for Weyl fillings
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        towardWeylStandard T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling,, 
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, mapping WeylFillings
        T' to integer coefficients, with $\sum_{T'} H(T') \cdot T' = T$ in the
        Weyl module and every key T' strictly larger than T in the term order
        used by *note weylStraighten: weylStraighten,

Description
===========

If T is already Weyl-standard the output is the singleton {T => 1}.  Otherwise
towardWeylStandard performs one divided-power Garnir shuffle across the first
violation (located by *note isWeylStandard: isWeylStandard,) and returns the
resulting linear combination.  Repeated application terminates at a
$\mathbb{Z}$-linear combination of Weyl-standard fillings; this is exactly what
*note weylStraighten: weylStraighten, computes.

The replacements are generated by divided-power comultiplication (see *note
divComult: divMult,) followed by divided-power multiplication (see *note
divMult: divMult,); the coefficients are products of binomial coefficients, so
in general towardWeylStandard produces many terms unlike the sign-flip shuffle
on the Schur side.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = weyl {{1,2},{0,0}}                                            |
|                                                                       |
|     +-+-+                                                             |
|o1 = |1|2|                                                             |
|     |0|0|                                                             |
|     +-+-+                                                             |
|                                                                       |
|o1 : WeylFilling                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isWeylStandard T                                                  |
|                                                                       |
|o2 = (0, 0)                                                            |
|                                                                       |
|o2 : Sequence                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : a = towardWeylStandard T                                          |
|                                                                       |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|o3 = HashTable{|0|0| => -1}                                            |
|               |1|2|                                                   |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|               |0|1| => -1                                             |
|               |0|2|                                                   |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|               |0|2| => -1                                             |
|               |0|1|                                                   |
|               +-+-+                                                   |
|                                                                       |
|o3 : HashTable                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : scan(pairs a, (U, c) -> << "  " << c << " * " << toList U << endl)|
|  -1 * {{0, 2}, {0, 1}}                                                |
|  -1 * {{0, 1}, {0, 2}}                                                |
|  -1 * {{0, 0}, {1, 2}}                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note WeylFilling: WeylFilling, -- a Young tableau stored row-wise for the
    Weyl-module basis
