      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rank of the underlying
        module
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the character, as a
        symmetric polynomial in $x_0, \ldots, x_{d-1}$, of the composed Weyl
        functor on the defining representation

Description
===========

The Weyl analogue of *note character: character,, using *note weyl: weyl,
instead of *note schur: schur,.  Over a field of characteristic zero
$W_\lambda(V) \cong S_\lambda(V)$ canonically, so weylCharacter returns the
same polynomial as character; this routine is provided for uniformity and for
verifying that the diagonal-character computation goes through the Weyl-side
construction end-to-end.

