weylModulesMap -- build a map between Weyl modules from its action on tableaux
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        weylModulesMap(N, M, F)
  * Inputs:
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a Weyl module from *note
        weylModule: weylModule,
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a Weyl module from *note
        weylModule: weylModule,
      * F, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function such that for
        every Weyl-semistandard filling T in the basis of M, F(T) produces a
        list of pairs (c, T') with c in ring N and T' a
        (not-necessarily-standard) filling of the shape of N
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the $R$-linear map M -> N whose
        value on each basis tableau is straightened into N

Description
===========

The Weyl analogue of *note schurModulesMap: schurModulesMap,.  The shape of N
is the target shape of the tableaux produced by F; the straightening into the
Weyl-standard basis is performed internally using *note weylStraighten:
weylStraighten,.

Example: a multiplication-style map $W_{(2)}(E) \to W_{(2,1)}(E) \otimes E^*$.
The analogue of the Koszul differential, with divided-power multiplication:

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 3;                                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x_1..x_n];                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = weylModule({2}, R^n);                                          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : N = weylModule({2,1}, R^n);                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = T -> apply(numgens R, k -> (R_k, augmentWeylFilling(T, 1, k)));|
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : weylModulesMap(N, M, F)                                            |
|                                                                        |
|o6 = | x_2 -x_1 0    0    0    0    |                                   |
|     | x_3 0    0    -x_1 0    0    |                                   |
|     | 0   x_2  -x_1 0    0    0    |                                   |
|     | 0   x_3  0    0    -x_1 0    |                                   |
|     | 0   0    x_3  0    -x_2 0    |                                   |
|     | 0   0    0    x_2  -x_1 0    |                                   |
|     | 0   0    0    x_3  0    -x_1 |                                   |
|     | 0   0    0    0    x_3  -x_2 |                                   |
|                                                                        |
|             8      6                                                   |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

